  "script": "What would happen if a package could get from New York to LA in 15 minutes? Right now, ground shipping takes about 5 days. Even a plane needs 6 hours. So trucks are out. Throwing it is out too. The longest throw on record is about 445 feet, and a box is worse. So, you build a catapult. Half a mile long. The box pulls about 2,400 Gs on the way out. It leaves at 14,000 miles an hour. That's 18 times the speed of sound. The bubble wrap does not make it. It clears the atmosphere and peaks around 600 miles up. Higher than the Space Station. Tracking says: in transit. Halfway there, it coasts over Kansas. A farmer looks up, and decides not to tell anyone. It comes down in Los Angeles, 15 minutes after launch. Right on time. The box arrives... mostly. It's dented, it's smoking, and someone still signs for it. And the shipping invoice? Still comes out right. Because Content Systems.ai checked every line.",
